──────────────────────────────────────────────
  SECTION 0: NAVIGATION BAR
  Role: Wayfinding + Primary CTA access
──────────────────────────────────────────────

  Layout:
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ [Logo]     Services   Work   About   Blog   Contact    [CTA]   │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Behavior:
  - Transparent on hero, becomes solid on scroll (glass-morphism blur)
  - Shrinks slightly on scroll (height: 80px → 64px)
  - "Services" has a mega-dropdown with icons + descriptions
  - "About" links to about/team/culture
  - CTA button: "Start a Project" — always visible, brand purple
  - Dark mode toggle (sun/moon icon)
  - Mobile: hamburger → full-screen overlay menu with staggered animations

  Psychology:
  - CTA visible at ALL times = zero-friction conversion path
  - Limited nav items (Hick's Law) = fast decision-making
  - Mega-menu shows depth of services without overwhelming

  File: src/components/layout/header.tsx
  Dependencies: src/constants/navigation.ts, src/hooks/useScrollPosition.ts


──────────────────────────────────────────────
  SECTION 1: HERO
  Role: Instant identity + emotional hook
  Time Budget: 3 seconds to hook
──────────────────────────────────────────────

  Layout:
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                                                                  │
  │                                                                  │
  │         We Design & Build                                        │
  │         Websites That                                            │
  │         Actually Convert.                      [Abstract         │
  │                                                 3D/Gradient      │
  │         RapSora is a web development            Visual or        │
  │         agency crafting digital                  Animated         │
  │         experiences that drive                  Element]         │
  │         real business growth.                                    │
  │                                                                  │
  │         [ View Our Work ]   [ Start a Project → ]               │
  │                                                                  │
  │                        ↓ Scroll                                  │
  │                                                                  │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Content Strategy:
  - Headline: Big, bold, benefit-driven (NOT "Welcome to RapSora")
    Options:
    a) "We Design & Build Websites That Actually Convert."
    b) "Digital Experiences That Move Your Business Forward."
    c) "We Build Websites Your Competitors Wish They Had."

  - Subheadline: One sentence, plain English, what-you-get
    "A web development agency crafting premium digital experiences
     that turn visitors into paying customers."

  - Two CTAs (split intent):
    PRIMARY:   "Start a Project →"  (high-intent leads)
    SECONDARY: "View Our Work"       (still exploring)

  Typography:
  - Headline: font-satoshi, 56-80px, font-bold, leading-tight
  - Subheadline: font-inter, 18-20px, text-muted-foreground, max-w-lg
  - Responsive: scales down proportionally on mobile

  Visual Element (RIGHT SIDE):
  - Option A: Abstract purple gradient blob with subtle animation
  - Option B: Masked video loop showing website builds
  - Option C: 3D floating geometric shapes (purple-themed)
  - The visual should NOT compete with the headline
  - It should create atmosphere, not distract

  Animation Choreography:
  1. Headline words reveal one-by-one (staggered, 80ms delay each)
  2. Subheadline fades in 400ms after headline completes
  3. CTAs slide up from bottom with spring physics
  4. Visual element has a slow, ambient floating animation (infinite)
  5. Scroll indicator pulses gently at the bottom

  Psychology:
  - "Actually Convert" — directly addresses the pain point
  - Two CTAs = captures both hot leads AND researchers
  - Big typography = confidence, authority
  - Animation = "these people know motion design"

  File: src/components/sections/hero.tsx
  Estimated time: 3-4 hours (get this perfect)


──────────────────────────────────────────────
  SECTION 2: LOGO MARQUEE / SOCIAL PROOF BAR
  Role: Instant trust through association
──────────────────────────────────────────────

  Layout:
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  Trusted by teams who take their brand seriously                 │
  │  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
  │  [Logo] [Logo] [Logo] [Logo] [Logo] [Logo] →→→ (infinite loop)  │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Behavior:
  - Infinite horizontal scroll (CSS-only, no JS for perf)
  - Logos in monochrome (grayscale), subtle hover → brand color
  - Small section, high density of logos
  - A thin separator line between headline and logos

  Content:
  - 8-12 client/partner logos
  - If no real logos yet, use industry-relevant text:
    "startups · saas · ecommerce · fintech · healthcare"

  Psychology:
  - Appears immediately after hero = "others trust them"
  - Monochrome logos = clean, non-competing with brand
  - Infinite scroll = suggests many clients (abundance)

  File: src/components/sections/logo-marquee.tsx
  Estimated time: 1 hour


